      {
        "id": 99258,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-16T05:27:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If the images you have are exactly what you want to print (with the black border the correct size), you'll need to add more border.</p><p>Sounds really weird, but PS requires an extra 36 pixels on all four sides, just in case the die miscuts slightly or something.</p><p>Here's how I do it in GIMP (Photoshop or other image programs are likely similar). Increase canvas size by 72px in both directions, centering the original - that makes a 36px border. Fill the border in black. Done!</p><p>When you upload to PS the card should now fit perfectly - don't worry about the low resolution warning if you know your images are high enough res, I guess PS can get confused by images that aren't photos even if they're fine and will print perfectly.</p><p>Hope that helps!</p>",
